==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|id=place upon|:inh|enm:coveren<id:place upon>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|coveren}}, borrowed from {{der|en|fro|covrir|covrir, cueuvrir}} (modern {{cog|fr|couvrir}}), from {{der|en|la-lat|coperire}}, from {{der|en|la|cooperiō|t=to cover completely}}, from {{m|la|co-|pos=intensive prefix}} + {{m|la|operiō|t=to close, cover}}. Displaced native {{cog|enm|thecchen}} and {{m|enm|bithecchen|bethecchen|t=to cover}} (from {{cog|ang|þeccan}}, {{m|ang|beþeccan|t=to cover}}), {{cog|enm|helen|helen, (over)helen, (for)helen|t=to cover, conceal}} (from {{cog|ang|helan|t=to conceal, cover, hide}}), {{cog|enm|wreon|wrien, (be)wreon|t=to cover}} (from {{cog|ang|wreon|(be)wrēon|t=to cover}}), {{cog|enm|hodren|hodren, hothren|t=to cover up}} (from {{cog|nds|hudren|t=to cover up}}).

According to the [[w:Oxford English Dictionary|Oxford English Dictionary]], the original sense of the verb and noun {{m|en|cover}} was “hide from view” as in its [[cognate]] {{m|en|covert}}. Except in the limited sense of “cover again”, the word {{m|en|recover}} is unrelated and is cognate with {{m|en|recuperate}}. Cognate with {{cog|es|cubrir}} and {{cog|pt|cobrir}}.

