===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[lid]].
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} Area or situation which screens a person or thing from [[view]].
#: {{ux|en|The soldiers took '''cover''' behind a ruined building.}}
# The front and back of a [[book]], [[magazine]], [[compact disc|CD]] [[package]], etc.
# The top [[sheet]] of a [[bed]].
# A cloth or similar material, often fitted, placed over an item such as a [[car]] or [[sofa]] or food to protect it from dust, rain, insects, etc. when not being used.
# {{lb|en|India}} A [[bag]] or [[packet]].
# A [[cover charge]].
#: {{ux|en|There's a $15 '''cover''' tonight.}}
# A [[setting]] at a [[restaurant]] table or formal [[dinner#Noun|dinner]].
#: {{ux|en|We need to set another '''cover''' for the Smith party.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=1|passage=When I gave a dinner there was generally a '''cover''' laid for him. I liked the man for his own sake, and even had he promised to turn out a celebrity it would have had no weight with me.}}
# {{lb|en|music}} A new performance or [[rerecording]] of a previously recorded song; a [[cover version]]; a [[cover song]].
# {{lb|en|cricket}} A [[fielding]] [[position]] on the [[off]] side, between [[point]] and [[mid off]], about 30° [[forward]] of [[square]]; a [[fielder]] in this position.
#: {{ux|en|The captain signalled his best fielder from short leg to '''cover'''.}}
# {{lb|en|cricket}} A [[tarpaulin]] or other [[device]] used to cover the [[wicket]] during [[rain]], to prevent it getting [[wet]].
#: {{ux|en| The '''covers''' were put on just before lunch.}}
# {{lb|en|cricket}} The area of the stumps that is blocked by the batsman so as to defend the wicket.
# {{lb|en|cricket}} A backup incase any player sustains injury during nets or midseries. Originally have to be declared part of squad before match.
#: {{ux|en| He was brought in as '''cover''' for wicketkeeper.}}
# {{lb|en|combinatorics|topology}} A [[collection]] (or ''[[family]]'') of subsets of a given set, whose union contains every element of said original set.
#: {{hyponyms|en|exact cover|partition}}
#: {{ux|en|The open intervals are a '''cover''' for the real numbers.}}
# {{lb|en|philately}} An [[envelope]] complete with [[stamp]]s and [[postmark]]s etc.
# {{lb|en|military}} A [[solid]] [[object]], including [[terrain]], that provides [[protection]] from [[enemy]] fire.
# {{lb|en|legal}} In [[commercial law]], a buyer’s [[purchase]] on the open market of [[goods]] similar or identical to the goods contracted for after a seller has [[breach]]ed a [[contract]] of sale by failure to deliver the goods contracted for.
# {{lb|en|insurance}} An insurance contract; [[coverage]] by an insurance contract.
# {{lb|en|espionage}} A [[persona]] maintained by a spy or undercover operative; [[cover story]].
# {{lb|en|dated}} A [[swindler]]'s [[confederate]].
# The portion of a slate, tile, or shingle that is hidden by the [[overlap]] of the [[course]] above.<ref>{{R:Knight AMD}}</ref>
# In a [[steam engine]], the [[lap]] of a [[slide valve]].
# {{lb|en|construction}} The distance between [[reinforcing]] [[steel]] and the exterior of [[concrete]].

