From {{inh|en|enm|crasshen}}, {{m|enm|crasschen|}}, {{m|enm|craschen||to break into pieces}}, of uncertain origin. Perhaps from a variant of earlier {{m|enm|*crasken}}, from {{suffix|enm|crasen|t1=to break|k|pos2=formative suffix|nocat=1}}; or from earlier {{m|enm|*craskien}}, {{m|enm|*craksien}}, a variant of {{m|enm|craken||to crack, break open}} (for form development compare {{m|en|break}}, {{m|en|brask}}, {{m|en|brash}}).

