===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# Reliance on the truth of something said or done; faith; trust.
#* {{RQ:KJV|1 Maccabees|10|46|passage=When Jonathan and the people heard these words they gave no '''credit''' into them, nor received them.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[recognition|Recognition]], [[respect]] and [[admiration]].
#: {{syn|en|due}}
#: {{ux|en|I give you '''credit''' for owning up to your mistake.}}
#: {{ux|en|He arrived five minutes late, but to his '''credit''' he did work an extra ten minutes at the end of his shift.}}
#* {{RQ:Cowper John Gilpin|page=343|passage=John Gilpin was a citizen <br> Of '''credit''' and renown, <br> A train-band Captain eke was he <br> Of famous London town.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1946|month=July and August|author=Cecil J. Allen|title=British Locomotive Practice and Performance|journal=Railway Magazine|page=213|text=The admirable smoothness of the riding also reflected the greatest '''credit''' on those who, despite the difficulties caused by the shortage of men and materials, have succeeded in maintaining the track in such first-class order.}}
