#* {{quote-book|en|author=Brian Carter; Justin Levy|title=Facebook Marketing|year=2012|publisher=Que Publishing|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=D8ryhTPgJzYC&lpg=PA178&dq=facebook%20%22credits%22&pg=PA178#v=onepage&q&f=false|isbn=978-0-7897-4113-4|page=178|passage=Facebook Credits are a virtual currency used only on Facebook that debuted in May 2009. Ten '''credits''' are equal to one dollar. Facebook keeps 30% of all Facebook Credit transactions.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} Recognition for having taken a course (class).
#: {{ux|en|If you do not come to class, you will not get '''credit''' for the class, regardless of how well you do on the final.}}
