##: {{syn|en|court of justice|tribunal|Thesaurus:court of law}}
##: {{ux|en|The '''court''' started proceedings at 11 o'clock.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=21 August 2012|author=Ed Pilkington|newspaper=The Guardian| title=[http://www.guardian.co.uk/world/2012/aug/21/death-penalty-trial-reggie-clemons?newsfeed=true Death penalty on trial: should Reggie Clemons live or die?]| passage=Next month, Clemons will be brought before a '''court''' presided over by a "special master", who will review the case one last time. The hearing will be unprecedented in its remit, but at its core will be a simple issue: should Reggie Clemons live or die?}}
##* {{quote-web|en|year=1985|title=''Criminal Code'' (R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46)|url=https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/c-46/page-140.html|work=Justice Canada|accessdate=1 March 2020|text=536(2.1). ... You have the option to elect to be tried by a provincial court judge without a jury; or you may elect to be tried by a judge without a jury; or you may elect to be tried by a '''court''' composed of a judge and jury.}}
## An organization for the administration of law, consisting of a body of judges with a certain jurisdiction along with its administrative apparatus.
##: {{ux|en|Each province in Canada has three '''courts''': a provincial '''court''', a superior '''court''', and a '''court''' of appeals.}}
## {{lb|en|often capitalized}} The judge or judges or other judicial officer presiding in a particular matter, particularly as distinguished from the counsel or jury, or both.
##* {{quote-web|en|title=''Gordon v. Canada,'' 2017 FC 454 |author=Kevin R. Aalto|url=https://www.canlii.org/en/ca/fct/doc/2017/2017fc454/2017fc454.html|work=CanLII|date=5 May 2017|accessdate=23 February 2020|text=A case conference in person was convened.... To emphasize that it was a Court proceeding the '''Court''' was gowned.}}
##* {{quote-web|en|title=''R. v. Carlson,'' 2018 BCPC 209|author=M.F. McParland|url=https://www.canlii.org/en/bc/bcpc/doc/2018/2018bcpc209/2018bcpc209.html|work=CanLII|date=17 August 2018|accessdate=1 March 2020|text=[5]... defence alleges there is a reasonable apprehension of bias based on the cumulative effect of several issues including the following: (1) The '''Court''' was “crying” during the victim impact statement; (2) The '''Court''' laughed or “scoffed” when defence stated its sentencing position; ...(6) The '''Court'''’s tone, facial expression and demeanor throughout the proceedings...}}
## The session of a judicial assembly.
##: {{ux|en|The '''court''' is now in session.}}
##* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.cbsnews.com/minnesota/live-updates/julissa-thaler-sentenced-murder-6-year-old-son-eli-hart/|title=Julissa Thaler sentenced to life in prison for murdering 6-year-old son, Eli Hart|author=WCCO Staff|date=2023-02-16|work=cbsnews.com|text=On Thursday morning, a Hennepin County judge formally sentenced Julissa Thaler to the life sentence for Eli Hart's murder. {{...}} After '''court''', family said their focus now turns to fundraising a playground in Mound in Eli Hart's honor {{...}}|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260421175608/https://www.cbsnews.com/minnesota/live-updates/julissa-thaler-sentenced-murder-6-year-old-son-eli-hart/|archivedate=21 April 2026}}
## Any [[jurisdiction]], civil, military, or ecclesiastical.
# {{senseid|en|sports}} {{lb|en|sports}} A place arranged for playing the games of [[tennis]], [[basketball]], [[handball]], [[badminton]], [[volleyball]], [[squash]] and some other games
#: {{ux|en|The local sports club has six tennis '''courts''' and two squash '''courts'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The shuttlecock landed outside the '''court'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1935|author=[https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/288354.George_Goodchild George Goodchild]| title=Death on the Centre Court| chapter=5| passage=By one o'clock the place was choc-a-bloc. […] The restaurant was packed, and the promenade between the two main '''courts''' and the subsidiary '''courts''' was thronged with healthy-looking youngish people, drawn to the Mecca of tennis from all parts of the country.}}
## one of the two divisions of a [[tennis]], badminton or volleyball court, in which the player or players of each team play
##* {{quote-text|en|year=2010|author=Cara Marcus|title=Faulkner Hospital
|passage=The photograph at left captures a great serve by Dr. Sadowsky, who will never forget one of Bobby Riggs's serves, which had such a great spin that it landed in his '''court''' and bounced back to the other side of the net before he had a chance to return it.}}
# {{lb|en|ornithology}} A space prepared and decorated by certain [[bird]] species in which to [[advertise]] themselves for a [[mate]].
#: {{ux|en|The male [[Wilson's bird of paradise]] clears an area of rainforest to create a '''court''' in which to perform an elaborate mating dance.}}

