===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[coppice#Noun|coppice]]: an area of [[woodland]] managed by [[coppice#Verb|coppicing]] (periodic cutting near stump level).
#: {{syn|en|mott}}
# Any [[thicket]] of small trees or shrubs, [[coppiced]] or not.
#: {{syn|en|thicket|bush|orchard}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1578|by={{w|Rembert Dodoens}}|translator={{w|Henry Lyte (botanist)|Henry Lyte}}|title=A niewe Herball or Historie of Plantes|original=Cruydeboeck|page=57|passage=Agrimonie groweth in places not tylled, in rough stone mountaynes, in hedges and '''Copses''', and by waysides.}}
#* {{RQ:Wordsworth Coleridge Lyrical Ballads|page=202|poem=Lines composed a few miles above Tintern Abbey|passage=The day is come when I again repose<br/>Here, under this dark sycamore, and view<br/>These plots of cottage-ground, these orchard tufts,<br/>Which at this season, with their unripe fruits,<br/>Among the woods and '''copses''' lose themselves,}}
#* {{RQ:Tennyson Poems 1833|page=109|title=The Lotos-Eaters|passage=Three thundercloven thrones of oldest snow, / Stood sunsetflushed: and, dewed with showery drops, / Upclomb the shadowy pine above the woven '''copse'''.}}
